# Testing and Definition of Done

- Test behavior through public domain, port, application, and core interfaces; do not couple tests to private runtime state.
- Unit tests cover schemas, policy, StepMeter, Budget, evidence normalization, proofs, gates, serializer purity, and redaction.
- Contract tests cover every Port, null adapter, CompetitionAdapter, output contract, provider manifest, and off/shadow equivalence.
- Scenario tests model `state + TypedAction → next state + Receipt` and cover pagination, popup/frame, stale refs, recovery, no-progress, and non-idempotent reconciliation.
- Fault tests cover model timeout, 429/5xx, malformed output, CDP disconnect, page crash, Worker SIGKILL, OOM, disk failure, JSONL half-lines, artifact failure, memory failure, and secret injection.
- Passive Replay must be deterministic after normalization. Live Provider runs are statistical and must not assert byte-identical traces.
- Every production failure becomes a minimized fixture with a bug-specific assertion at the first divergent event.
- Do not update expected outputs merely to accept a changed implementation; explain the contract change first.
- Tests must assert receipts, trace events, evidence, gates, or terminal states—not only “no exception”.
- A task is complete only when targeted tests pass and applicable architecture, type, lint, and contract checks have run.
